00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:20.120
Hisabisa no doraibu de minna hai tenshon

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.384
Hisabisa no doraibu de minna hai tenshon

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:25.254
Kare mo kuru no

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:28.855
Myaku ga ima wa nakutomo

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:32.596
Zettai ikimasu tomo

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:38.637
Sugoi sugoi pookaa faisu dato shitara

00:00:39.406 --> 00:00:41.775
Aru yo nante

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:45.845
Umi wa hiyake suru kara, yama ni shiyou tte

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:48.814
Umi wa hiyake suru kara, yama ni shiyou tte

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:53.953
Koo-to no kisetsu nanoni kanchigai shiteru

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:58.390
Koo-to no kisetsu nanoni kanchigai shiteru

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:02.629
Doushite nano?

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:06.599
Konna ureshikute

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:14.404
Chigiresouna hodo waratte iru noni

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:22.949
Kare no senaka mite wa mune tsumaru

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:30.913
Taenai egao no utsu no naka de

00:01:33.059 --> 00:01:36.995
Episode #12
His Thoughts

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:53.876
Hey, Kate!

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:56.850
What?

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:59.385
Why in the world would you
squeeze this many lemons?

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:01.321
I'm supplementing my vitamin intake.

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:02.413
Something you wanted?

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:04.657
Remember when we were out for
diner the other night

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:06.750
and we ran into Emilio's friend?

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:09.153
Huh? Oh, yeah...

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:13.430
Um... Yeah, Herve! You remember him, right?

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.134
Yeah... Why's that?

00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:19.530
Well, it turns out that he wants
to meet you again.

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:21.373
Really?!

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:29.772
It'll be fine. I won't do anything to make them
suspicious and I won't say anything.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:32.511
I'm just going to observe the enemy.

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:36.322
If that's so, why do you insist
on meeting her like this?

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:38.158
There must be some other way.

00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:39.386
There isn't.

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:42.624
I promise, I won't do anything to Kate.

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:45.557
And you can keep seeing Emma
as you have been.

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:46.966
But...

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:48.801
If I can observe her surroundings,

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.970
I think I might be able to get to the
source of things and find out

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:55.236
who controls her,
who it is that gives their orders.

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:57.243
It's too dangerous.

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:58.578
Well, I'm going to ask...

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:00.705
What kind of a future do you see
for Emma and yourself?

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:04.384
Don't you want to be together forever?

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:06.085
Haven't you ever thought about getting married?

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:06.753
Yeah, I have...

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:07.153
Well then, don't you think your current situation
Yeah, I have...

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:09.255
Well then, don't you think your current situation

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:11.191
is awfully dangerous?

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:13.318
I mean, you have no idea when
you might manifest!

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:16.961
It's the same for my sister and me.

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:19.390
We live life not knowing when
we might manifest!

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:24.302
Emilio, don't you want to put
an end to this life of fear?

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:27.774
As long as our bodies are
controlled by this curse,

00:03:27.774 --> 00:03:30.038
our futures will never hold anything but sorrow.

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:31.939
Herve...

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:35.548
I want to be rid of this burden.

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:36.783
And if you can be rid of it too,

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:40.685
you could lead a normal life and
be together with Emma forever.

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:45.346
I plan to do whatever I must so that I
can be together with those I love!

00:03:46.526 --> 00:03:50.656
Emilio, that is what you must do too.

00:03:51.231 --> 00:03:52.532
Don't you think?

00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:53.829
That's incredible!

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:01.174
I don't even know why I do it.

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:02.508
What do you mean?

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:06.410
I guess I just try to avoid getting
into the relationship too deep.

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:07.547
Huh?

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:10.880
I bet it's because of having this new body.

00:04:11.351 --> 00:04:14.514
It's like I'm scared someone might
notice if they touch me.

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:16.656
Oh...

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:19.759
But at the same time, I want
to be together with him.

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:21.060
A contradiction like that...

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:23.722
I know he would never understand, but...

00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:26.466
You just want to be with him even more.

00:04:26.466 --> 00:04:27.490
Exactly!

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:30.464
The closer you get, the more you
have to keep some distance.

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:32.097
Isn't it awful?

00:04:33.706 --> 00:04:35.208
Yeah, you might just have a point.

00:04:35.208 --> 00:04:36.376
Huh?

00:04:36.376 --> 00:04:39.038
For some odd reason, people push those
away that show them kindness.

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:42.115
I mean Yuan's left me,
as one might have expected...

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:43.683
Huh? Really?

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:47.744
But don't you think you were maybe
being a little too stubborn?

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:49.455
No, not at all.

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:52.356
Okay, so you told Yuan you found a job then?

00:04:52.792 --> 00:04:53.693
No...

00:04:53.693 --> 00:04:54.694
Well then?

00:04:54.694 --> 00:04:56.195
Hey, it's him that's avoiding me.

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:58.561
But you should tell him...

00:04:58.798 --> 00:04:59.599
What?

00:04:59.599 --> 00:04:59.966
I think he'd be happy to hear about it,
What?

00:04:59.966 --> 00:05:02.935
I think he'd be happy to hear about it,

00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:04.232
if he were to hear it from you.

00:05:05.104 --> 00:05:06.939
What the hell do you know about it?

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:08.508
Well, I...

00:05:08.508 --> 00:05:11.170
Well, Rose just might have a point there.

00:05:11.344 --> 00:05:14.881
Huh? What is it with all of you?

00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:17.907
Claire, isn't Yuan always there for you?

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:20.845
I've got to admit, I'm a little jealous.

00:05:21.254 --> 00:05:22.744
What are you talking about?!

00:05:23.156 --> 00:05:25.317
That dude isn't there for me period.

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:28.016
Even if it's just for a little while, doesn't it bother
you when he's not there for you?

00:05:28.328 --> 00:05:29.095
Huh?

00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:29.395
That's right.
Huh?

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:30.293
That's right.

00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:32.665
That kind of relationship must be nice.

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:35.532
For sure! I'm so jealous!

00:05:37.904 --> 00:05:39.806
What do you guys know?!

00:05:39.806 --> 00:05:42.570
Me, I've never had any relationships.

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:45.311
How about you, Kate?

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:47.541
Aren't you interested in any guys?

00:05:48.681 --> 00:05:51.484
Um, well...

00:05:51.484 --> 00:05:52.685
Huh? Is there someone?!

00:05:52.685 --> 00:05:56.314
Well, I mean, there's this guy I'm
going to meet up with, but...

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:58.450
Really?

00:05:58.658 --> 00:05:59.659
Are you serious?!

00:05:59.659 --> 00:06:02.362
It's nothing to be so surprised about.

00:06:02.362 --> 00:06:04.197
But it's surprising, isn't it?!

00:06:04.197 --> 00:06:05.565
C'mon, let's have the details!

00:06:05.565 --> 00:06:09.092
Well, I don't really know what to think, but...

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:11.628
But?

00:06:11.971 --> 00:06:16.442
Until now, I'd never have thought
about doing so, but...

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:17.568
But?

00:06:17.877 --> 00:06:22.576
Well, I just figure that if I'm going have
an experience, now is the time.

00:06:23.716 --> 00:06:25.017
You plan on getting him in bed?!

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:26.452
No! Not at all!

00:06:26.452 --> 00:06:30.115
I just thought that maybe I should
start trying to date a little bit.

00:06:30.523 --> 00:06:32.692
Oh, that's what you meant.

00:06:32.692 --> 00:06:34.093
Thank God!

00:06:34.093 --> 00:06:36.596
Well, it might be a good change for you.

00:06:36.596 --> 00:06:37.995
I wonder?

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:41.226
Yeah, it might be good for you.

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:44.103
This party is going to be totally off the hook!

00:06:44.103 --> 00:06:46.906
Yeah, and that place is so cool!

00:06:46.906 --> 00:06:48.641
Really?!
Oh yeah?!

00:06:48.641 --> 00:06:51.010
That's why I'm saying you should go too, Luke!

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:52.612
Huh? Oh, yeah.

00:06:52.612 --> 00:06:55.672
Just being seen at an event like
this will bring good things!

00:06:55.815 --> 00:06:58.551
And recently the owner of Abbas was there!

00:06:58.551 --> 00:07:02.688
Yeah, I know! That place is booked
solid three months deep!

00:07:02.688 --> 00:07:05.122
Yeah, good thing we had connections
or we'd never have gotten in!

00:07:07.593 --> 00:07:09.829
It was to die for!

00:07:09.829 --> 00:07:11.097
So, their food's really that good?

00:07:11.097 --> 00:07:13.332
It's incredible! You'd be totally amazed.

00:07:13.332 --> 00:07:15.535
Yeah? Well, why didn't you invite me then?!

00:07:15.535 --> 00:07:18.404
Sorry, we could hardly fit around
the table as it was.

00:07:18.404 --> 00:07:20.373
It's true, there wasn't any more room.

00:07:20.373 --> 00:07:23.910
Ah! You girls always keep the
best stuff to yourselves!

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:26.379
Hey, Luke, we should go to that party!

00:07:26.379 --> 00:07:28.614
We'll show our faces and
if it sucks we can just leave.

00:07:28.614 --> 00:07:29.449
Yeah...

00:07:29.449 --> 00:07:31.050
C'mon, you didn't invite me!

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:33.041
You'll end up there even if we
don't take you with us!

00:07:33.252 --> 00:07:34.754
You'll end up there even if we tell you not to!

00:07:34.754 --> 00:07:35.788
What?!

00:07:35.788 --> 00:07:36.880
Luke!

00:07:37.089 --> 00:07:38.858
Ah, Rachel!

00:07:38.858 --> 00:07:41.027
Rachel, we were looking for you!

00:07:41.027 --> 00:07:43.596
What are you doing? C'mon, let's
all head back together!

00:07:43.596 --> 00:07:44.722
Luke?!

00:07:45.364 --> 00:07:47.559
Sorry, wait for me at the bus stop!

00:07:50.336 --> 00:07:53.533
So, have those two been having their
share of problems lately?

00:07:53.973 --> 00:07:56.609
Who knows. Let's go.

00:07:56.609 --> 00:07:59.479
Huh, they're having lots of problems?

00:07:59.479 --> 00:08:01.347
Give it up, Sam. You don't stand a chance.

00:08:01.347 --> 00:08:02.548
What? I don't know what you mean.

00:08:02.548 --> 00:08:04.050
It couldn't be more obvious.

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:06.085
I never said I liked her!

00:08:06.085 --> 00:08:07.553
You totally dig her!

00:08:07.553 --> 00:08:09.111
You think I dig her?

00:08:11.224 --> 00:08:13.993
I tried to call you several times last night.

00:08:13.993 --> 00:08:15.688
Oh yeah?

00:08:16.062 --> 00:08:17.997
I even left a message.

00:08:17.997 --> 00:08:21.334
Oh, I didn't notice it until the morning.

00:08:21.334 --> 00:08:23.769
Yeah, I just had a lot of stuff going on.

00:08:23.769 --> 00:08:24.895
I see...

00:08:26.973 --> 00:08:29.809
Luke, about last night...

00:08:29.809 --> 00:08:31.037
That? It's fine.

00:08:31.277 --> 00:08:33.246
I'm sure you've got a lot going on too.

00:08:33.246 --> 00:08:34.914
Luke, it's not that...

00:08:34.914 --> 00:08:37.041
Let's just forget about that for now.

00:08:38.251 --> 00:08:39.377
Luke...

00:08:39.619 --> 00:08:41.287
I'll call you tonight.

00:08:41.287 --> 00:08:42.388
Tonight?

00:08:42.388 --> 00:08:44.690
Yeah, later...

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:45.558
Really?

00:08:45.558 --> 00:08:46.820
For sure.

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:49.189
Well, everyone's waiting for me.

00:08:56.836 --> 00:09:00.101
Since it's this late, the store probably
doesn't even have bread left.

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:02.975
You're probably right. Want to drop by a chafe?

00:09:02.975 --> 00:09:03.942
Okay...

00:09:10.917 --> 00:09:11.918
Hey, Yuan!

00:09:11.918 --> 00:09:12.852
Wh... What?!

00:09:12.852 --> 00:09:14.114
Why are you avoiding me?!

00:09:14.654 --> 00:09:15.755
You're coming with me.

00:09:15.755 --> 00:09:16.756
What?!

00:09:16.756 --> 00:09:17.590
Just come on!

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:18.682
Hey!

00:09:19.792 --> 00:09:20.860
What do you want?

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:23.195
How long are you going to keep avoiding me?!

00:09:23.195 --> 00:09:24.964
It's not like I'm trying to avoid you.

00:09:24.964 --> 00:09:26.866
You have something that you
want to say to me?!

00:09:26.866 --> 00:09:28.527
No, I don't.

00:09:30.236 --> 00:09:33.103
You're an awful liar,
and you're just pissing me off more!

00:09:33.773 --> 00:09:35.207
You just can't take the middle ground, can you?

00:09:35.207 --> 00:09:37.004
So, what do you want me to do?!

00:09:37.376 --> 00:09:39.105
Just be normal!

00:09:41.013 --> 00:09:43.811
But, Claire, you're so tense lately.

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:47.486
I just thought I'd give you some
space until you find a job.

00:09:47.486 --> 00:09:49.221
Did I ever ask for space?

00:09:49.221 --> 00:09:50.188
Huh?

00:09:50.656 --> 00:09:52.749
It irritates me when you do that.

00:09:53.392 --> 00:09:54.381
Oh...

00:09:54.894 --> 00:09:58.352
Well, you should come by again for
a Super Royal with cheese.

00:09:58.931 --> 00:10:02.168
Huh? But I thought you quit your job there?

00:10:02.168 --> 00:10:03.903
Well, I'm working there again.

00:10:03.903 --> 00:10:07.273
Really?! No way! At that hamburger stand?!

00:10:07.273 --> 00:10:08.407
Yeah...

00:10:08.407 --> 00:10:10.309
But I thought you said you couldn't
stand that old guy.

00:10:10.309 --> 00:10:13.112
Well, you said I should give that
place another shot, so I did!

00:10:13.112 --> 00:10:14.880
You're kidding me! No lie?!

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:16.682
Huh? Really?!

00:10:16.682 --> 00:10:18.484
Claire, that's great!

00:10:18.484 --> 00:10:19.585
C'mon, you don't have to scream it!

00:10:19.585 --> 00:10:24.156
Well, I'll be damned... Really!

00:10:24.156 --> 00:10:25.646
What's the big deal?

00:10:37.903 --> 00:10:42.237
I decided to dismiss the disciplinary
committee's decision on your case.

00:10:42.875 --> 00:10:43.876
What?

00:10:43.876 --> 00:10:46.012
I used my veto power.

00:10:46.012 --> 00:10:49.815
So, you can continue on with your
duties as a part of Grace

00:10:49.815 --> 00:10:50.950
just as you always have.

00:10:50.950 --> 00:10:53.976
But I...

00:10:54.253 --> 00:10:55.655
And when you have other things
that you need to do,

00:10:55.655 --> 00:10:57.390
it's all right to give those things priority.

00:10:57.390 --> 00:10:58.324
What?

00:10:58.324 --> 00:11:02.818
I'll take care of things.
So, please don't quit Grace.

00:11:03.162 --> 00:11:04.697
Paula...

00:11:04.697 --> 00:11:08.997
I don't know what kind of problems
you're dealing with right now,

00:11:09.769 --> 00:11:14.399
but I think that being a part of Grace means
everything to you at this school.

00:11:14.807 --> 00:11:18.265
Everything to me at this school...

00:11:19.078 --> 00:11:21.672
And I think you know that it does too.

00:11:22.314 --> 00:11:25.442
So for now, just don't make any rash decisions.

00:11:26.852 --> 00:11:30.413
Let's stick this out together. Please?

00:11:33.526 --> 00:11:34.925
Okay...

00:11:55.381 --> 00:11:56.177
Bobby!

00:12:03.989 --> 00:12:07.526
This girl too, look at her body
and her last photo.

00:12:07.526 --> 00:12:09.895
It's like there's a time slip or something.

00:12:09.895 --> 00:12:15.527
And there's more. This girl too...
this girl too... this girl too...

00:12:16.969 --> 00:12:18.664
There are so many contradictions, aren't there?

00:12:19.038 --> 00:12:21.307
You think the autopsies are inaccurate?

00:12:21.307 --> 00:12:24.071
You think Alan would make this
many mistakes in a row?

00:12:24.310 --> 00:12:26.437
No, you've got a point there.

00:12:27.279 --> 00:12:29.081
But why then?

00:12:29.081 --> 00:12:31.417
The girls' corpses appear younger
that than they do

00:12:31.417 --> 00:12:33.749
in the last pictures taken of them
when they were alive!

00:12:34.987 --> 00:12:37.148
I know, that's what I'm trying to figure out.

00:12:38.758 --> 00:12:39.925
Let's roll.

00:12:39.925 --> 00:12:41.358
Huh? Where?

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:43.687
You and I have got some facts to set straight.

00:12:46.832 --> 00:12:50.870
Is there anything that you need?
Just tell me if you do, okay?

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:52.238
I'm fine.

00:12:52.238 --> 00:12:54.840
Isn't there anything that Paul or Carrie want?

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:56.569
I said we're fine, Mom.

00:12:56.709 --> 00:12:59.610
We've have everything one needs to get by.

00:13:00.012 --> 00:13:01.380
Really...

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:05.874
Rose, I'm so sorry that you've had
do to all this work for me.

00:13:07.286 --> 00:13:10.050
I'm having fun with it, so you
don't have to worry yourself.

00:13:10.289 --> 00:13:11.557
Really?

00:13:11.557 --> 00:13:14.794
To tell the truth, I've been getting
some money from your father

00:13:14.794 --> 00:13:15.954
the over the past few months.

00:13:16.996 --> 00:13:19.765
From Dad? Really?

00:13:19.765 --> 00:13:23.758
I take it as proof that he's got
himself a job somewhere.

00:13:24.503 --> 00:13:25.538
Yeah...

00:13:25.538 --> 00:13:27.640
He's caused us all trouble,

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:31.201
but in his own way, I think he's trying his best.

00:13:31.811 --> 00:13:33.245
You're probably right.

00:13:33.245 --> 00:13:37.375
Maybe he asked the company he used to
work for to help him find a job.

00:13:42.254 --> 00:13:44.056
And that's when your began your career there?

00:13:44.056 --> 00:13:45.691
Yeah, effectively.

00:13:45.691 --> 00:13:48.751
The project was in its final stage,
and I just didn't have time for her.

00:13:49.128 --> 00:13:51.163
So, what did she do then?

00:13:51.163 --> 00:13:54.291
She got angry and sick of it all,
then one day she just disappeared.

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:56.001
So, you were dumped?

00:13:56.001 --> 00:13:57.662
Yep, just thrown away.

00:13:57.903 --> 00:13:59.972
Seems a little suspect to me.

00:13:59.972 --> 00:14:00.673
Why's that?

00:14:00.673 --> 00:14:01.207
I think there's more to this story
than you're telling us.
Why's that?

00:14:01.207 --> 00:14:02.541
I think there's more to this story
than you're telling us.

00:14:02.541 --> 00:14:03.676
Sis!

00:14:03.676 --> 00:14:04.810
For instance?

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:06.712
Well, something more complicated.

00:14:06.712 --> 00:14:10.349
Ah, yeah, I may have abridged that part.

00:14:10.349 --> 00:14:11.617
I thought so!

00:14:11.617 --> 00:14:13.686
You don't need to pry like that.

00:14:13.686 --> 00:14:14.820
No, that's fine.

00:14:14.820 --> 00:14:16.021
It's understandable that your sister

00:14:16.021 --> 00:14:17.886
wants to conduct a little
background check on me.

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:19.391
Yeah, that's all!

00:14:19.391 --> 00:14:22.528
Well, seeing as Herve's been drilled
with questions all night,

00:14:22.528 --> 00:14:24.257
shall we call it an evening?

00:14:25.030 --> 00:14:26.465
Is it that late already?

00:14:26.465 --> 00:14:28.234
It's still kind of early.

00:14:28.234 --> 00:14:30.102
Yeah, I suppose...

00:14:30.102 --> 00:14:31.303
Yeah!

00:14:31.303 --> 00:14:36.508
Hey, would it be all right if I were
to walk Kate home later?

00:14:36.508 --> 00:14:37.376
Huh?!
Um...

00:14:37.376 --> 00:14:40.579
Herve! I mean, you just met her.

00:14:40.579 --> 00:14:41.807
You'd rather not?

00:14:43.315 --> 00:14:45.180
Kate, what do you want to do?

00:14:45.684 --> 00:14:46.919
I, um...

00:14:46.919 --> 00:14:47.987
So, it's okay then?

00:14:47.987 --> 00:14:50.389
Huh? Well...

00:14:50.389 --> 00:14:51.583
It's all right?

00:14:52.524 --> 00:14:53.459
Sure.

00:14:53.459 --> 00:14:55.361
But they just met and...

00:14:55.361 --> 00:14:56.328
It's fine, don't you think?

00:14:56.328 --> 00:14:58.564
From here on out, they can decide what
they want to do themselves.

00:14:58.564 --> 00:15:01.124
Yeah, well, I suppose...

00:15:03.969 --> 00:15:04.837
Herve...

00:15:04.837 --> 00:15:05.771
Huh?

00:15:05.771 --> 00:15:08.073
We had said that all four of us were
going to stick together today.

00:15:08.073 --> 00:15:09.108
Did we?

00:15:09.108 --> 00:15:11.911
Don't act like you don't know!
What are you planning on doing?

00:15:11.911 --> 00:15:14.013
Walking her home, that's all.

00:15:14.013 --> 00:15:15.180
Really?

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:16.340
Ah, here we go.

00:15:19.985 --> 00:15:20.753
Herve...

00:15:20.753 --> 00:15:21.053
It's fine, don't worry.
Herve...

00:15:21.053 --> 00:15:22.816
It's fine, don't worry.

00:15:26.458 --> 00:15:27.893
What's wrong?

00:15:27.893 --> 00:15:29.828
Is something worrying you?

00:15:29.828 --> 00:15:32.998
Uh, no, I'm just kind of in a daze.

00:15:32.998 --> 00:15:36.490
Well, he seems like a pretty nice guy.

00:15:36.835 --> 00:15:38.393
Yeah, yes.

00:15:38.671 --> 00:15:40.472
And it looks like Kate likes him too.

00:15:40.472 --> 00:15:41.440
You think so?

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:45.536
There's no way that girl would have decided
to be alone with him if she didn't.

00:15:50.649 --> 00:15:53.140
I wouldn't have expected to find Kate
out for a walk with some guy.

00:15:53.485 --> 00:15:55.612
Yeah, that's not her style.

00:15:55.988 --> 00:15:57.182
Huh?!

00:15:57.556 --> 00:15:58.691
What?

00:15:58.691 --> 00:16:01.489
She's right at that age where she'll
want to have new experiences.

00:16:01.961 --> 00:16:05.164
But that guy, I wonder where she found him?

00:16:05.164 --> 00:16:07.333
I think it was him that found Kate.

00:16:07.333 --> 00:16:08.567
He found her?!

00:16:08.567 --> 00:16:09.935
Why not?

00:16:09.935 --> 00:16:11.630
You mean she's actually his type?

00:16:12.805 --> 00:16:15.140
What's wrong with there being
guys into girls like that?

00:16:15.140 --> 00:16:16.375
I suppose...

00:16:16.375 --> 00:16:19.378
Listen to you, you're really being quite rude.

00:16:19.378 --> 00:16:20.579
But...

00:16:20.579 --> 00:16:22.748
Well, which of them do you think
would be your type?

00:16:22.748 --> 00:16:23.816
Me? Well...

00:16:23.816 --> 00:16:25.017
Tell me, who?

00:16:25.017 --> 00:16:27.577
Um, Claire, I suppose...

00:16:29.288 --> 00:16:31.153
Ah, they're coming this way.

00:16:36.762 --> 00:16:39.498
Actually, there were some girls
from my neighborhood

00:16:39.498 --> 00:16:41.367
who went to the same school as you,

00:16:41.367 --> 00:16:43.995
and one of them was in Grace.

00:16:44.236 --> 00:16:45.404
Really?

00:16:45.404 --> 00:16:47.929
People around her used to look
at her in a different light.

00:16:48.574 --> 00:16:50.943
Everyone thought she was a genius,
a prodigy even.

00:16:50.943 --> 00:16:52.877
I remember how she always
got special treatment.

00:16:53.245 --> 00:16:55.347
Don't you think you're maybe
exaggerating a bit?

00:16:55.347 --> 00:16:59.518
No, her parents were always
bragging about her.

00:16:59.518 --> 00:17:02.688
When I'd pass by them in the street,
they'd hide her behind them

00:17:02.688 --> 00:17:05.816
and glare at me like,
"Don't even think about touching her."

00:17:06.592 --> 00:17:08.994
Don't you think there might have been
another problem at play?

00:17:08.994 --> 00:17:10.291
No way!

00:17:10.529 --> 00:17:12.520
Now that I think about it,
what a terrible story to tell!

00:17:13.699 --> 00:17:17.658
Well, I think I've come a long way
since then, don't you?

00:17:18.303 --> 00:17:22.467
I mean, here I am walking the streets at
night with a member of Grace.

00:17:22.641 --> 00:17:23.801
Oh...

00:17:24.877 --> 00:17:27.413
I wanted your sister to like me so I
played the good-guy role tonight,

00:17:27.413 --> 00:17:29.005
and I think it's paid off.

00:17:29.281 --> 00:17:30.182
Huh?

00:17:30.182 --> 00:17:32.946
I'm not exactly the person I probably
came off as tonight.

00:17:33.519 --> 00:17:35.054
Is that so?

00:17:35.054 --> 00:17:37.147
I might be a really dangerous guy.

00:17:38.323 --> 00:17:41.053
I don't think that's true, but...

00:17:41.493 --> 00:17:42.653
Why's that?

00:17:43.429 --> 00:17:46.330
I think you're kind. It's in your eyes.

00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:51.092
Well, it's just a feeling I have.

00:17:51.570 --> 00:17:54.664
I bet you have a younger brother
or sister, don't you?

00:17:54.873 --> 00:17:56.534
Yeah, why do you ask?

00:17:57.309 --> 00:18:00.801
I just had a feeling. A younger sister?

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:02.440
I thought so!

00:18:02.848 --> 00:18:05.050
You fill the two requirements.

00:18:05.050 --> 00:18:06.285
I read it in a book.

00:18:06.285 --> 00:18:10.278
Someone with kindness in their eyes that has a
younger sister is not a dangerous person.

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:13.954
Or maybe that's just what I want to believe!

00:18:19.765 --> 00:18:22.201
Gimme a Super Royal with cheese!

00:18:22.201 --> 00:18:23.293
Comin' up!

00:18:30.742 --> 00:18:32.141
Oh, damn!

00:18:33.278 --> 00:18:35.940
Sorry it got a little late.
Is your sister going to mind?

00:18:36.248 --> 00:18:39.084
No, it'll be fine.

00:18:39.084 --> 00:18:40.051
Good.

00:18:40.519 --> 00:18:41.286
Well, bye.

00:18:41.286 --> 00:18:41.620
Wait.
Well, bye.

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:42.348
Wait.

00:18:42.654 --> 00:18:45.390
Would you be interested in getting
together again on Sunday?

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:46.391
What?

00:18:46.391 --> 00:18:47.459
You don't want to?

00:18:47.459 --> 00:18:49.862
No, it's not that. It's just...

00:18:49.862 --> 00:18:50.920
It's just?

00:18:51.830 --> 00:18:54.799
Don't you think I'm kind of boring to be with?

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:56.235
Why do you say that?

00:18:56.235 --> 00:19:01.172
I don't have anything interesting to say,
and I'm kind of boring.

00:19:01.673 --> 00:19:03.809
No, I had a great time tonight!

00:19:03.809 --> 00:19:05.003
Really?

00:19:05.244 --> 00:19:06.404
Really!

00:19:06.612 --> 00:19:08.842
So, are you free this coming Sunday?

00:19:09.414 --> 00:19:10.415
Sunday?

00:19:10.415 --> 00:19:12.542
What do you say to heading
out to Coney Island?

00:19:12.918 --> 00:19:15.045
To Coney Island?

00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:18.280
Yeah, they've got these great hot dogs there!

00:19:18.957 --> 00:19:20.792
The thing is, like, this long

00:19:20.792 --> 00:19:23.158
and they top it with this super-spicy chili sauce!

00:19:24.496 --> 00:19:27.124
Huh? What's so funny?

00:19:27.900 --> 00:19:29.067
It's just not what I'd expect of you.

00:19:29.067 --> 00:19:30.068
Really?

00:19:30.068 --> 00:19:33.595
Yeah, I think I'd like to give one a try too!

00:19:33.839 --> 00:19:34.999
Cool, it's a date!

00:19:35.274 --> 00:19:36.041
Yeah.

00:19:36.041 --> 00:19:36.575
Let's exchange phone numbers,
Yeah.

00:19:36.575 --> 00:19:37.940
Let's exchange phone numbers,

00:19:38.210 --> 00:19:39.575
then I'll pick you up at your place on Sunday.

00:19:39.945 --> 00:19:40.912
Sure!

00:19:45.851 --> 00:19:46.585
Hello?

00:19:46.585 --> 00:19:47.152
Luke? It's me...
Hello?

00:19:47.152 --> 00:19:48.954
Luke? It's me...

00:19:48.954 --> 00:19:50.353
Oh, hi.

00:19:50.722 --> 00:19:53.592
What are you doing now? You at home?

00:19:53.592 --> 00:19:58.029
I was, but now I'm hanging
in the neighborhood.

00:19:58.463 --> 00:19:59.865
Oh, you're out.

00:19:59.865 --> 00:20:00.899
Yeah.

00:20:00.899 --> 00:20:03.835
I was just waiting. You said you'd call.

00:20:03.835 --> 00:20:06.338
Oh, sorry, I was going to, but...

00:20:06.338 --> 00:20:08.774
Luke, look at this.
Don't you think this one's nicer?!

00:20:08.774 --> 00:20:10.207
Um, I'm sorry, I'm a little...

00:20:14.079 --> 00:20:15.410
Amanda...

00:20:19.384 --> 00:20:23.753
So, is Herve being a decent
conversation partner?

00:20:24.423 --> 00:20:26.323
Um, yeah...

00:20:26.825 --> 00:20:29.419
So, seen any good movies lately?

00:20:30.696 --> 00:20:31.964
You don't remember?

00:20:31.964 --> 00:20:35.331
You know, something that had you on
the edge of your seat or moved you?

00:20:36.835 --> 00:20:37.402
Um...

00:20:37.402 --> 00:20:37.936
Herve, don't talk about stuff like that yet.
Um...

00:20:37.936 --> 00:20:39.871
Herve, don't talk about stuff like that yet.

00:20:39.871 --> 00:20:42.669
Well, if I don't know anything about her,
it's pointless to spend time with her!

00:20:45.577 --> 00:20:47.179
I think that's good for today.

00:20:47.179 --> 00:20:49.170
Ah! Thank God!

00:20:49.481 --> 00:20:50.846
See you tomorrow.

00:20:51.783 --> 00:20:52.718
Okay...

00:20:52.718 --> 00:20:55.520
Oh yeah, what about trying to keep a diary?

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:57.055
Maybe it would help you remember things.

00:20:57.055 --> 00:20:58.023
Herve!

00:20:58.023 --> 00:20:59.786
Maybe I'll try keeping one too.

00:21:00.325 --> 00:21:03.192
If I can manage it, maybe we could
even exchange them, you think?

00:21:03.395 --> 00:21:05.297
Exchange diaries?

00:21:05.297 --> 00:21:07.162
Herve! That's enough!

00:21:12.838 --> 00:21:15.773
Exchange diaries?

00:21:19.678 --> 00:21:21.305
Screw that stupid experiment.

00:21:28.954 --> 00:21:31.390
My only love sprung from my only hate

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:33.792
Too early seen unknown, and known too late

00:21:33.792 --> 00:21:38.729
Prodigious birth of love it is to me,
that I must love a loathed enemy

00:21:39.131 --> 00:21:41.566
Step by step kimi to deatte
Step by step, I lost track of time

00:21:41.566 --> 00:21:44.136
Toki wo wasurete odoriakashita
And kept on dancing when I met you

00:21:44.136 --> 00:21:46.438
Hoshi ni yadoru sadame wo shirazu ni
Without knowing the fate that lies in the stars

00:21:46.438 --> 00:21:48.974
I can't stop falling in love

00:21:48.974 --> 00:21:51.543
Fujitsu na tsuki no kaketa moraru ni
An unfaithful moon's lacking morals

00:21:51.543 --> 00:21:53.879
Terasareru no wa michita desire
Give light to my full-on desire

00:21:53.879 --> 00:21:56.248
Sadame wo daita boku wa sakenda
Grasping onto fate I scream out

00:21:56.248 --> 00:21:58.817
"Wherefore art thou Juliet?"

00:21:58.817 --> 00:22:00.614
Oroka na koi dato
Go ahead and laugh at it

00:22:01.119 --> 00:22:02.950
Azawarau ga iisa
And call it stupid love

00:22:03.555 --> 00:22:05.523
Subete nagedashite
Throw it all

00:22:06.024 --> 00:22:07.958
Ima sugu ni yuku kara
Because I'll be right there

00:22:08.627 --> 00:22:10.993
Oh, my Juliet...

00:22:11.063 --> 00:22:15.434
Ne kamisama oshiete yo
Tell me God, what do I do

00:22:15.434 --> 00:22:20.667
Dou sureba negai wa kanau
To make my wishes come true?

00:22:21.006 --> 00:22:25.310
Ah! Konnani setsunakute
Ah! This is so painful

00:22:25.310 --> 00:22:28.211
Yozora ni naku yo
I howl into the night sky

00:22:29.648 --> 00:22:36.355
Ne dare mo ga konna omoi wo daite
Does everyone go to sleep

00:22:36.355 --> 00:22:39.591
Nemuri ni tsuku no
Holding onto a thought like this?

00:22:39.591 --> 00:22:43.895
Ah! Ima sugu me wo samashite
Ah! Open your eyes right away

00:22:43.895 --> 00:22:46.732
Uso dato waratte yo
Laugh at it if it's a joke

00:22:46.732 --> 00:22:49.166
Oh, my sweet Juliet

00:22:50.802 --> 00:22:53.271
Nemureru kimi to na mo naki boku wa
You who's sleeping and I with no name

00:22:53.271 --> 00:22:54.773
Higeki no ame ni utare
Pelted by tragic rain

00:22:54.773 --> 00:22:56.434
Say good die

00:23:02.447 --> 00:23:05.814
The first invitation...
Their time together...

00:23:06.885 --> 00:23:09.755
Then, in one place, all thoughts get knotted up.

00:23:09.755 --> 00:23:11.857
Episode #13
Holiday
Then, in one place, all thoughts get knotted up.

00:23:11.857 --> 00:23:14.451
Episode #13
Holiday
